WEBVTT

00:00.940 --> 00:04.230
The sword fighting tournament... 
Good thing the weather's fair.

00:05.010 --> 00:10.400
<i>Lady Rudolvon said she and Princess Mia 
would make lunch for Prince Sion...</i>

00:12.020 --> 00:14.860
Why do I feel this strange unease?

00:14.860 --> 00:18.520
It somehow feels like... 
danger looms for my master.

01:51.000 --> 01:52.790
Oh, Mr. Keithwood.

01:51.000 --> 01:56.420
<b>Episode 6: The Sword Fighting Tournament:
Prince Abel's Fight</b>

01:52.790 --> 01:54.630
Are you hungry?

01:54.630 --> 01:56.880
Princess Mia, what is that?

01:58.490 --> 02:00.640
So kind of you to ask.

02:00.640 --> 02:03.480
A creation into which I poured my all:

02:04.010 --> 02:06.060
horse bread!

02:07.550 --> 02:08.730
<i>Horse?</i>

02:08.730 --> 02:13.580
Prince Abel just adores horses, 
so I'm sure he'll be delighted!

02:13.580 --> 02:17.650
I-It's true that a fundamental aspect 
of cooking is considering the diner,

02:18.260 --> 02:20.910
but this bread has a fatal flaw!

02:23.020 --> 02:26.730
If it's a horse, the ears 
should be more like this.

02:27.870 --> 02:29.300
Not that!

02:29.300 --> 02:32.710
If it's this big, the heat won't 
reach the center of the dough!

02:32.710 --> 02:33.540
Make it roughly

02:33.540 --> 02:35.920
this size!

02:35.920 --> 02:37.630
My magnum opus!

02:37.630 --> 02:41.100
Mr. Keithwood, what do you 
think of my vegetables?

02:41.100 --> 02:41.900
Yes?

02:42.990 --> 02:46.470
It would appear you're quite skilled at
 cutting vegetables, Lady Rudolvon.

02:46.470 --> 02:50.440
Yes! I can handle any slicing and dicing!

02:50.750 --> 02:54.800
However, neither Prince Sion nor 
Prince Abel are herbivores,

02:54.800 --> 02:57.250
so I'm not certain they can 
eat this much cabbage.

02:57.250 --> 03:00.950
Is it really too much? 
Isn't this a normal amount?

03:00.950 --> 03:02.820
<i>In what circumstances is this normal?</i>

03:05.330 --> 03:06.990
This appetizing smell is...

03:07.530 --> 03:09.460
Meat! Cooked!

03:11.380 --> 03:16.300
M-My... this is cooked... 
q-quite nicely, Miss Liora.

03:16.300 --> 03:19.420
Yes! I cook in courtyard!

03:19.420 --> 03:20.960
How... outdoorsy...

03:20.960 --> 03:22.760
Please just use an oven!

03:23.080 --> 03:27.220
He's right, Miss Liora. 
We're cooking for princes.

03:27.220 --> 03:30.240
<i>Now there's the common sense I would expect</i>

03:30.240 --> 03:32.060
<i>from someone whose family runs a trade group.</i>

03:32.490 --> 03:34.100
<i>She even brought a book.</i>

03:34.350 --> 03:37.760
According to <i>Exquisite Dishes! 
Recipes for Little-Explored Delicacies</i>,

03:37.760 --> 03:41.630
the best way to bring out the 
ingredients' flavor is with raw meat.

03:41.630 --> 03:44.070
Absolutely not! Please don't follow that!

03:44.070 --> 03:48.260
Oh, but I think they would 
enjoy horse liver sashimi.

03:48.260 --> 03:52.620
Serving horse to a member of the 
equestrian club is out of the question!

03:54.000 --> 03:56.830
<i>The situation is even more 
dire than I anticipated.</i>

03:56.830 --> 03:59.380
<i>If they continue on this course...</i>

03:59.880 --> 04:02.380
Tons of cabbage

04:00.380 --> 04:02.380
Underbaked

04:00.880 --> 04:02.380
Raw meat
(liver)

04:05.370 --> 04:07.050
Princess and ladies!

04:08.290 --> 04:11.010
Listen carefully to what I'm about to say.

04:11.500 --> 04:13.800
We're going to make simple 
sandwiches for these lunches.

04:13.800 --> 04:14.900
Is that clear?

04:15.880 --> 04:18.980
Are you sure it wouldn't be better 
to make something more elaborate?

04:19.470 --> 04:21.750
Is. That. Clear?

04:23.290 --> 04:26.400
In that case, you can handle 
the dough, Princess Mia.

04:26.400 --> 04:29.290
Normal, rectangular bread will suffice.

04:29.290 --> 04:31.120
Leave it to me!

04:31.380 --> 04:34.830
Mr. Keithwood, is this what 
you had in mind for the salad?

04:34.830 --> 04:38.040
As I expected from you, 
Lady Rudolvon. Excellent work.

04:38.620 --> 04:42.010
<i>I just hope it's a normal amount of food...</i>

04:42.390 --> 04:45.770
Mr. Keithwood, the dough is ready.

04:45.770 --> 04:47.470
Then let's get it in the oven—

04:53.680 --> 04:55.390
A horse, again.

04:59.690 --> 05:02.280
<i>I know I said to make it rectangular!</i>

05:02.650 --> 05:08.530
<i>Mia's head had been too full of thoughts of Abel, 
so she didn't hear that key detail.</i>

05:08.530 --> 05:10.930
What do you think, Mr. Keithwood?

05:11.860 --> 05:16.630
We're making sandwiches, woman! How are we 
gonna fit the ingredients between these?

05:17.110 --> 05:18.960
<i>That's how I feel. But...</i>

05:22.230 --> 05:24.320
Yes, that will do.

05:27.880 --> 05:28.550
Great!

05:29.460 --> 05:33.270
They're finished! Our specially 
made horse sandwiches!

05:33.530 --> 05:35.580
We managed to make it work.

05:35.580 --> 05:38.450
Good job, everyone. You worked very hard.

05:38.450 --> 05:43.360
<i>Needless to say, 
Keithwood worked the hardest.</i>

05:43.600 --> 05:45.040
Mr. Keithwood.

05:46.020 --> 05:48.550
You were of great help 
to us on this occasion.

05:48.550 --> 05:50.280
We appreciate it.

05:50.540 --> 05:51.380
Oh.

05:51.920 --> 05:53.750
That's very kind of you.

05:53.750 --> 05:56.100
I will pass on your regards to Prince Sion.

05:56.100 --> 06:01.010
You misunderstand. I'm expressing 
appreciation not to Prince Sion but to <i>you</i>.

06:01.010 --> 06:02.000
To me?

06:02.250 --> 06:06.420
It's thanks of you that we were 
able to make these lunches.

06:06.420 --> 06:09.570
So, thank you very much.

06:10.430 --> 06:14.690
<i>Nobles don't normally bow 
their heads to servants.</i>

06:14.690 --> 06:19.100
<i>However, Princess Mia doesn't allow 
herself to be trapped by that convention.</i>

06:19.100 --> 06:22.650
<i>She willingly expresses thanks to everyone.</i>

06:22.900 --> 06:24.320
<i>You see,</i>

06:24.320 --> 06:27.490
<i>while I would express
thanks to Mr. Keithwood,</i>

06:27.490 --> 06:31.540
<i>I flatly refuse to express 
thanks to </i>Prince Sion.

06:31.540 --> 06:37.250
<i>Keithwood would never have dreamed 
what Mia was actually thinking.</i>

06:41.430 --> 06:44.500
It's as if the entire town 
moved into the campus grounds!

06:44.770 --> 06:47.090
Princess Mia and Lady Chloe.

06:47.390 --> 06:50.340
I bought these from one of the stalls.

06:51.860 --> 06:53.840
Oh, my. Thanks, Anne.

06:53.840 --> 06:55.440
Thank you.

06:55.440 --> 06:57.190
These look scrumptious.

06:57.190 --> 06:58.230
Let's see...

06:58.230 --> 06:59.610
P-Princess Mia!

07:03.190 --> 07:05.820
Th-The part you just ate was...

07:05.820 --> 07:07.030
red pepper!

07:08.800 --> 07:10.280
Spicy!

07:10.280 --> 07:13.200
Too spicy!

07:13.200 --> 07:15.550
H-Help! Does anyone have some water?

07:15.550 --> 07:16.660
Take this.

07:19.870 --> 07:23.670
Th-Thank you so... much?

07:24.950 --> 07:26.430
Prince Abel!

07:26.430 --> 07:28.240
I'm glad I could be of assistance.

07:28.240 --> 07:30.050
Excuse us...

07:30.290 --> 07:33.260
<i>Prince Abel somehow seems...</i>

07:33.540 --> 07:35.720
Well, if it isn't Princess Mia.

07:36.280 --> 07:40.320
Oh, you're Prince Abel's older brother.

07:40.320 --> 07:42.810
I'm honored you remember me.

07:43.090 --> 07:47.470
By the way, I hear you made 
my brother a lunch for today.

07:47.470 --> 07:50.530
Yes. I put my all into making it.

07:51.170 --> 07:53.740
My, what a pity that is.

07:54.000 --> 07:55.600
A pity?

07:55.600 --> 07:56.740
Well, you see,

07:56.740 --> 08:00.290
Abel's first opponent is me.

08:00.290 --> 08:03.960
In other words, 
he'll lose in the first match.

08:04.620 --> 08:08.670
I don't imagine the taste of 
defeat will enhance the meal.

08:08.670 --> 08:12.320
Still, I didn't expect you would 
fall in love with my brother.

08:12.320 --> 08:15.430
They may call you the Wisdom of the 
Empire, but you're still a child.

08:15.430 --> 08:17.760
That's why you have no eye for men.

08:17.760 --> 08:21.890
Brother! Don't say such 
disrespectful things to Princess Mia!

08:23.080 --> 08:27.690
<i>At the time, my priority 
was developing connections.</i>

08:29.140 --> 08:31.900
<i>But it seems I've inspired 
quite a grudge here.</i>

08:32.320 --> 08:38.620
<i>Antagonizing the first prince of the 
Kingdom of Remno doesn't seem wise...</i>

08:38.870 --> 08:41.770
<i>I think the move here is for Abel to lose,</i>

08:41.770 --> 08:44.360
<i>simultaneously restoring the 
older brother's self-esteem,</i>

08:44.360 --> 08:47.750
<i>and allowing me to deepen my relationship 
with Abel by comforting him.</i>

08:47.750 --> 08:49.050
<i>It's genius!</i>

08:49.050 --> 08:52.150
<i>The most important thing 
is avoiding the guillotine!</i>

08:53.000 --> 08:55.180
<i>So I'll just...</i>

08:58.200 --> 09:01.710
I have an opponent 
I desperately want to beat.

09:06.940 --> 09:10.360
Please win your match 
against him, Prince Abel!

09:10.580 --> 09:11.480
Huh?

09:11.940 --> 09:15.730
The taste of victory will make the 
lunch I made that much better!

09:18.130 --> 09:20.660
Yes, you're exactly right.

09:21.750 --> 09:23.580
What chummy lovebirds you are.

09:30.140 --> 09:33.130
We now begin match seven
 of the preliminaries!

09:39.770 --> 09:43.020
Well, let's see how much you've grown,

09:43.420 --> 09:45.180
my dear little brother!

09:50.860 --> 09:53.480
<i>He's strong... I knew he would be...</i>

09:53.770 --> 09:56.450
Hmm. So that's all you've got, is it?

09:56.450 --> 09:57.320
Then...

09:57.780 --> 09:59.740
Let's see how you like this!

10:05.120 --> 10:08.580
You've caught yourself quite 
the woman, haven't you, Abel?

10:08.850 --> 10:09.800
Huh?

10:09.800 --> 10:13.960
For a weakling like you to try to 
hook the princess of the empire...

10:13.960 --> 10:17.280
I'm sure Father will be overjoyed!

10:17.280 --> 10:18.680
What are you talking about?

10:18.680 --> 10:23.310
If you and that princess 
should ever get married,

10:23.310 --> 10:26.060
then I'll give her some strict 
discipline training for you.

10:26.430 --> 10:30.440
I'm sure a little pain will teach 
that princess some obedience!

10:33.900 --> 10:35.690
Brother!

10:36.110 --> 10:38.070
Why the scary look all of a sudden?

10:39.120 --> 10:42.090
You can say whatever you wish about me.

10:42.770 --> 10:43.530
However,

10:43.860 --> 10:48.370
if you insist on further 
disparaging Princess Mia...

10:49.340 --> 10:53.710
That's... the first stance in the 
Kingdom of Remno's swordsmanship.

10:55.330 --> 10:58.670
Let's say I keep disparaging her. Then what?

10:59.200 --> 11:00.130
Then I...

11:00.130 --> 11:01.340
I absolutely

11:02.300 --> 11:03.760
won't stand for it!

11:15.690 --> 11:17.150
Match over!

11:17.460 --> 11:20.360
Winner, Abel Remno!

11:23.690 --> 11:26.570
Prince Abel!

11:36.960 --> 11:38.420
I... won.

11:39.570 --> 11:42.970
That was truly amazing, Prince Abel!

11:42.970 --> 11:47.040
You defeated your brother in your first 
and won your second match, too!

11:47.040 --> 11:48.350
Very well done!

11:48.350 --> 11:51.270
Thanks. It was all thanks 
to you supporting me.

11:51.620 --> 11:54.520
No, this was all your efforts paying off!

11:54.520 --> 11:55.970
<i>If he's this strong,</i>

11:55.970 --> 12:00.140
<i>then maybe he can wipe the smirk 
off that stupid Prince Sion's face!</i>

12:01.650 --> 12:04.240
<i>Classic "relying on others to do it."</i>

12:04.500 --> 12:07.640
You very well could win 
the entire tournament!

12:07.640 --> 12:12.000
That may prove difficult. I have to 
contend with Prince Sion, after all.

12:12.000 --> 12:16.670
Have confidence in yourself. 
You're strong, Prince Abel!

12:16.670 --> 12:17.710
Princess Mia...

12:23.630 --> 12:24.900
Sorry to keep you waiting.

12:25.630 --> 12:28.070
P-Prince Sion?!

12:28.070 --> 12:33.160
Lady Rudolvon suggested we 
all enjoy lunch together.

12:33.840 --> 12:35.860
T-Tiona said that?!

12:36.580 --> 12:39.650
<i>Hold on. What are you making 
that "I did it" face for?</i>

12:40.000 --> 12:41.220
I hope we're not intruding.

12:41.220 --> 12:44.920
N-No. You're not intruding at all!

12:46.800 --> 12:51.210
<i>This jerk! After leaving me all 
alone in the previous timeline,</i>

12:51.210 --> 12:53.210
<i>what is this attitude about?</i>

12:53.470 --> 12:56.170
Oh, what interesting sandwiches.

12:56.410 --> 12:58.270
Are they shaped like horses?

12:59.120 --> 13:01.050
P-Prince Abel...

13:06.600 --> 13:09.430
It tastes wonderful, Princess Mia.

13:11.960 --> 13:14.680
I'm so glad to hear you like it!

13:14.680 --> 13:19.250
<i>That's right! The special feature of these 
sandwiches is that they're horse-shaped.</i>

13:19.250 --> 13:21.630
<i>That idea was all mine!</i>

13:21.630 --> 13:26.520
<i>So basically, all the praise for 
the sandwiches is praise for me!</i>

13:26.520 --> 13:28.910
<i>It's okay to cry, Keithwood.</i>

13:29.130 --> 13:33.530
Prince Abel, belated congratulations for 
your first victory against your brother.

13:33.530 --> 13:35.750
Thanks. It is so kind of you to go to the trouble.

13:35.750 --> 13:39.360
The truth is, I owe you an apology as well.

13:39.360 --> 13:40.250
An apology?

13:41.520 --> 13:45.590
I assumed you would lose.

13:45.590 --> 13:48.240
<i>Wow! How rude!</i>

13:48.240 --> 13:52.060
<i>Prince Abel could never lose 
to that lousy brother of his!</i>

13:52.340 --> 13:55.430
Don't apologize. You were 
correct to hold that opinion.

13:55.430 --> 13:57.890
I won because I got lucky.

13:57.890 --> 14:00.980
<i>Goodness me! Such modesty!</i>

14:01.410 --> 14:05.930
Luck still matters. I can't say all my 
wins were purely due to my skill, either.

14:05.930 --> 14:07.350
<i>That's right!</i>

14:07.350 --> 14:10.620
I'm honored to hear you 
say that, Prince Sion.

14:10.620 --> 14:13.950
<i>Having him acknowledge 
you isn't that big a deal!</i>

14:14.250 --> 14:15.160
Regardless,

14:15.820 --> 14:18.380
let's make our next match a good one.

14:19.740 --> 14:21.050
Of course.

14:21.050 --> 14:24.500
I feel fortunate to have the opportunity 
to spar with someone of your skill—

14:29.390 --> 14:30.490
<i>Princess Mia.</i>

14:31.020 --> 14:32.370
<i>I see.</i>

14:32.370 --> 14:37.680
<i>Princess Mia is telling me to 
stand proud. Message received!</i>

14:37.900 --> 14:44.370
<i>Prince Abel, you can ignore that jerk 
and laud my sandwiches some more.</i>

14:44.370 --> 14:48.400
<i>Princess Mia was simply trying 
to get more attention.</i>

14:48.910 --> 14:52.990
<i>Princess Mia believes in me.
 I won't let her down!</i>

14:52.990 --> 14:55.560
Come to the match prepared, Prince Sion.

14:56.530 --> 14:59.370
I don't intend to lose.

15:00.160 --> 15:02.920
<i>I'll win the match to repay 
Princess Mia's faith in me!</i>

15:03.920 --> 15:04.940
I see.

15:05.350 --> 15:08.760
Then I swear here and now to fight 
and defeat you with all I have.

15:09.070 --> 15:12.140
A passionate friendship has formed
 between these boys... Lovely!

15:12.450 --> 15:20.480
<i>U-Um... What happened to 
talking about my sandwiches?!</i>

15:20.790 --> 15:24.410
<i>Thus it was that lunch time passed.</i>

15:26.140 --> 15:28.920
Time to begin the next match!

15:30.610 --> 15:33.930
<i>Prince Abel, please win!</i>

15:33.930 --> 15:34.730
<i>Claim victory,</i>

15:35.280 --> 15:38.690
<i>and wipe the smirk off that jerk's face!</i>

15:38.690 --> 15:41.210
<i>A true small-fry line.</i>

15:45.340 --> 15:50.640
<i>Prince Sion is skilled 
at countering any attack.</i>

15:50.640 --> 15:54.390
<i>A style of swordsmanship an ordinary 
person like me can't hope to imitate.</i>

15:55.050 --> 15:55.850
<i>Still...</i>

15:58.330 --> 16:03.080
This is a stance passed down in the
 Kingdom of Remno called the first stance.

16:03.080 --> 16:06.770
It's a move adapted purely to 
striking faster than the opponent.

16:07.210 --> 16:09.480
The stance you used to 
defeat your brother, right?

16:09.830 --> 16:16.490
Yes. I poured heart and soul into training 
to swing my blade down faster and faster

16:17.240 --> 16:19.040
in order to beat you!

16:30.750 --> 16:33.010
<i>He's still beyond my reach?</i>

16:38.150 --> 16:40.650
<i>There was no counter?</i>

16:41.470 --> 16:45.200
<i>His Highness failed to unleash his counter...</i>

16:45.690 --> 16:50.030
<i>If you let your guard down, you'll get 
knocked off your feet, Prince Sion.</i>

16:51.180 --> 16:54.390
Didn't you say you weren't 
going to go easy on me?

16:54.390 --> 16:56.700
We both have our own 
circumstances to contend with.

16:57.340 --> 17:02.040
Whatever the case may be, 
my options are limited.

17:04.620 --> 17:09.100
<i>I didn't think I was underestimating 
Prince Abel, but I didn't expect this.</i>

17:09.800 --> 17:13.880
<i>The weight of his first strike 
left my arm numb.</i>

17:15.810 --> 17:17.550
<i>I haven't been pushed back like this,</i>

17:18.470 --> 17:21.260
<i>not since my training with my father!</i>

17:21.260 --> 17:27.980
<i>Prince Abel is managing to calmly analyze 
the skill gap between him and Prince Sion.</i>

17:22.320 --> 17:26.550
Ah, so close! Keep at it! Oh, again...

17:28.640 --> 17:33.170
<i>He's marching unwaveringly forward, 
knowing both himself and his opponent.</i>

17:33.170 --> 17:36.200
<i>Truly a kingly quality.</i>

17:36.510 --> 17:40.280
<i>And the one who set things in 
motion to turn out this way....</i>

17:41.280 --> 17:42.480
<i>That darn Sion!</i>

17:42.480 --> 17:46.090
<i>He keeps darting around! 
The impudent little...</i>

17:46.090 --> 17:49.380
<i>She sounds like a villain.</i>

17:52.980 --> 17:55.970
You can't win if all you 
do is dodge, Prince Sion.

17:56.450 --> 17:59.550
I expect it was Princess Mia 
that made you so strong.

18:00.080 --> 18:01.260
That's right.

18:01.830 --> 18:07.700
I used to tell myself it was impossible to 
overcome natural differences in ability.

18:07.700 --> 18:09.730
I was just running away from having to try.

18:10.710 --> 18:14.360
But after coming to Saint Noel Academy 
and meeting her...

18:15.070 --> 18:19.410
That day I felt, for the first time,
 a desire to beat you!

18:19.800 --> 18:23.620
Princess Mia believes in someone 
like me and asked me to win.

18:23.620 --> 18:26.200
Therefore, I can't afford to lose!

18:26.480 --> 18:27.560
I see.

18:27.560 --> 18:29.660
I'm a bit jealous.

18:29.660 --> 18:33.930
However, I can't afford to lose either!

18:37.200 --> 18:38.780
What? Rain?

18:38.780 --> 18:42.510
Princess Mia, you'll get soaked. 
Quickly, let's head to a covered area.

18:42.790 --> 18:45.540
I can deal with the rain.

18:45.540 --> 18:46.810
But...

18:46.810 --> 18:51.120
I need to witness this match 
all the way to the end.

18:51.120 --> 18:52.400
Princess Mia...

18:52.400 --> 18:55.400
Th-Then I'll go fetch an umbrella!

18:56.160 --> 18:58.780
<i>Witness the match, eh?</i>

18:58.780 --> 18:59.820
<i>In other words,</i>

18:59.820 --> 19:02.420
<i>she's attempting to use this match</i>

19:02.420 --> 19:06.120
<i>to awaken the talent she saw 
lying dormant within Prince Abel.</i>

19:06.570 --> 19:11.440
<i>As if I could let myself miss the moment 
Prince Abel wipes the floor with Sion!</i>

19:11.440 --> 19:13.540
<i>This is the reality.</i>

19:13.860 --> 19:19.640
<i>I see. She won't allow the talent 
sleeping within everyone to go to waste.</i>

19:19.640 --> 19:23.050
<i></i>This<i> must be the true
nature of the Wisdom of the Empire.</i>

19:23.050 --> 19:24.390
Here it comes!

19:38.380 --> 19:41.240
I see. So you've finally 
decided to get serious?

19:41.590 --> 19:43.450
I've been serious from the start.

19:44.020 --> 19:46.530
Your slashes are truly something.

19:47.040 --> 19:48.910
That's precisely why I warn you:

19:49.550 --> 19:53.250
If you try the same attack 
again, you'll lose.

19:53.470 --> 19:54.960
Is that so?

19:54.960 --> 20:00.220
Then in order to beat you, 
there's only one thing to do.

20:01.380 --> 20:05.650
<i>If I try to change my tactics now, 
I'll lose for certain.</i>

20:05.650 --> 20:09.020
<i>If my attack can't be the same 
as the ones I've been doing...</i>

20:09.490 --> 20:13.230
<i>Then you just have to unleash an 
attack that exceeds them, is that it?</i>

20:13.930 --> 20:15.980
Then I shall meet your attack!

20:16.380 --> 20:19.400
As a rival who owes you a 
clash with his full strength!

20:21.280 --> 20:22.740
Stop!

20:22.740 --> 20:27.330
Due to rain, the tournament 
is hereby suspended!

20:27.330 --> 20:28.790
What? Suspended?

20:29.760 --> 20:31.750
I feared that might happen.

20:31.750 --> 20:36.330
The purpose of the tournament is to 
deepen friendship between the students.

20:36.330 --> 20:37.720
The rain puts a damper on that.

20:37.720 --> 20:38.750
But I...

20:39.490 --> 20:43.970
I would love to settle this 
match some day, Prince Abel.

20:44.320 --> 20:48.260
Could we promise each other a rematch?

20:48.800 --> 20:50.510
Prince Sion...

20:51.680 --> 20:53.480
I'd like nothing more!

21:00.650 --> 21:02.660
Prince Abel!

21:02.660 --> 21:03.700
Princess Mia.

21:06.320 --> 21:09.910
You stayed out in the rain? We need 
to get you dry or you'll catch—

21:09.910 --> 21:11.290
That was amazing!

21:11.290 --> 21:15.750
You were so close! It ended right when
 you were just a step away from victory.

21:16.030 --> 21:19.870
N-No. If the match had gone on,
 I'm sure I would have—

21:19.870 --> 21:25.360
I bet some miserable person who didn't 
want you to win prayed for rain.

21:25.360 --> 21:30.160
How disgraceful of that person to 
pour cold water on your fair fight.

21:30.160 --> 21:35.250
<i>Coming from the person who did this
in the previous timeline:</i>

21:35.250 --> 21:38.710
<i>Having wound up alone during 
the tournament, Mia...</i>

21:38.710 --> 21:40.580
That blasted Prince Sion.

21:40.580 --> 21:44.970
You don't deserve victory 
after you rejected my lunch!

21:44.970 --> 21:47.950
I hope the tournament gets 
rained out so you can't win!

21:47.950 --> 21:51.360
Rain, heed my call! Let rain fall!

21:51.360 --> 21:55.190
<i>...resorted to this miserable, 
disgraceful behavior.</i>

21:55.190 --> 21:57.580
You were really only one step from winning!

21:57.580 --> 22:00.170
It's so frustrating! It makes me angry!

22:00.470 --> 22:04.920
Gosh darn it! The rain is a big dummy!

23:34.930 --> 23:39.930
Illustration by: chibi
